==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|maymen}}, {{m|enm|mahaymen}}, from {{etyl|xno|en}} {{m|fro|maheimer}}, {{m|fro|mahaigner}}, of {{etyl|gem|en}} origin; see [[mayhem]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|eɪm|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[wound]] seriously; to cause permanent loss of function of a limb or part of the body.
#*{{quote-book|year=1914|author={{w|Louis Joseph Vance}}
|chapter=1|title=[http://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/29671 Nobody]
|passage=Three chairs of the steamer type, all '''maimed''', comprised the furniture of this roof-garden, with (by way of local colour) on one of the copings a row of four red clay flower-pots filled with sun-baked dust from which gnarled and rusty stalks thrust themselves up like withered elfin limbs.}}

